      "text": "We start by letting $a=\\log_x 4$ and $b=\\log_{27} 3$.\nFrom property 2 of exponents in section 8.3, we know that $a-\\log_{27} 27=b$.\n\nNext, by property 1 in section 8.3, we know that $a=2\\cdot 2^{\\log_x 2}$.\n\nHence, $\\log_x 2^{\\log_x 2}=a$.\n\nAccording to one one-to-one correspondence between logarithms and exponential functions:\n$log_x 2^{log_x 2}=2.\\log_x 2^{log_x 2}$.\n\nSo $a^2=a$, which means $a=1$ or $a=0$.\n\n$\\log_x 2=2$ or $\\log_x 2=0$.\nTherefore:\n$x^2=4$ or $x^2=1$.\n$x=2$ or $x=-2$ or $x=\\pm 1$.\nFinally, we choose the positive solutions, so $x=\\boxed{2}$.The answer is: 2",
